Healthcare Interoperability Using FHIR
Overview
Healthcare organizations often use different Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems. Interoperability enables these systems to securely exchange patient information.

Key Technologies
Electronic Health Records (EHR)
Health Information Exchange (HIE)
HL7
FHIR (Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources)
Scenario
A patient receives treatment at Hospital A using Epic and later visits Hospital B using Cerner.

Using FHIR standards, healthcare data such as demographics, medications, allergies, laboratory results, and encounter information can be exchanged between systems.

Benefits
Improved patient care
Reduced duplicate testing
Better clinical decision-making
Improved care coordination
Enhanced patient safety
Challenges
Data privacy and security
Data quality issues
System compatibility
Implementation costs
Conclusion
FHIR plays an important role in helping healthcare organizations share patient information efficiently and securely.
